                <pb facs="0223" n="121" sameAs="frus:frus1919v01/pg121"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">715.1715/106: Telegram</note>
                <head><hi rendition="#italic">The Secretary of State to
                        the Consul in Charge of the Legation in Honduras</hi> (<hi rendition="#italic">Lawton</hi>)</head>
                <opener><dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Washington</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1919-12-11T15:00:00-05:00"><hi rendition="#italic">December 11,
                                1919, 3 p.m.</hi></date></dateline></opener>
                <p>Your December 4, 11 A.M., and Department’s Dec. 1, 2 P.M., inform Government of
                    Honduras that Department considers the installing of telegraph lines in the
                    disputed territory a violation of the <hi rendition="#italic">status quo</hi>
                    and such lines should therefore be removed. The Department has telegraphed
                    Legation at Managua to take up with Nicaraguan Government question of cutting
                    timber in disputed territory.</p>
                <closer><signed><hi rendition="#small-caps">Lansing</hi></signed></closer>
            </div>
